# Replacement rules for scripts/publish_clean.sh. Copy this file to scripts/publish_replacements.local
# (gitignored: the rules name what they replace) and replace the examples with the real rules.
# One rule per line, `regex:<python regex>==><replacement>`, applied in this order to every text file
# version and every commit message of the cleaned copy. Put longer forms before the shorter ones they
# contain. (?i) makes a rule ignore case. Never match anything the current tree still holds: the
# check wants the copy's tip to equal the source tip.

# Wording:
regex:<old phrase>==><new phrase>

# A machine's network route:
regex:<address pattern>==><address>

# Names: the longer path form first.
regex:(?i)<user>_<suffix>==><user>
regex:(?i)<user>==><user>
regex:(?i)<machine name>==><machine>
